	<key>readme</key>
	<string>Create a calendar event from one line of text.

Keyword: ev  (configurable)

Examples
  ev dentist tomorrow 2pm
  ev lunch with Jan fri 12:30 +1.5h @Downtown #work
  ev mom's birthday 5 dec          (no time = all day)
  ev meeting 25-11 at 9:30 until 11:00 #personal

Parts (in any order)
  Date: today, tomorrow, mon..sun, 25-11, 5 dec   (Dutch words work too)
  Time: 14:00, 2pm, 14.30, at 14:00
  End: until 15:00, or a duration: +1h, +30m, +1.5h
  Place: @Office (use underscores for spaces: @Main_Street)
  Calendar: #work (the start of the name is enough)

Enter creates the event in the calendar shown. Every writable calendar is listed as its own result, your default first. Cmd+Enter creates it and opens Calendar.</string>
